# shadcn UI Conventions

- Prefer existing shadcn components before custom styled markup.
- Compose primitives correctly (`DialogTitle` in dialogs, `TabsTrigger` inside `TabsList`, `AvatarFallback` in avatars).
- Use component variants and semantic tokens over ad-hoc class overrides.
- Use `cn()` for conditional classes; avoid complex manual string concatenation.
- For layout spacing, use `flex/grid` with `gap-*`; avoid legacy `space-x-*` / `space-y-*`.
- Keep forms structured with shared form primitives and consistent validation states.
- Keep icons consistent with project icon library and component composition rules.
- Preserve accessibility defaults (labels, aria attributes, keyboard navigation) when customizing components.
